surface-tangent-check.out
Analytical equilibria with finite-difference checks of membrane, fibre and bending material tangents
StaticStructural nsteps 2 deltat 1.0 maxiter 30 manrmsteps 1 rtolv 1.e-11 rtolf 1.e-11 nmodules 1
errorcheck
domain 3d
OutputManager tstep_all dofman_all element_all
ndofman 13 nelem 4 ncrosssect 4 nmat 4 nbc 11 nic 0 nltf 2 nset 10
# Each triangle has the target F = diag(1.1,1.2,0), with one free horizontal dof.
# The nodal force is half of the analytical P11 at that F (reference area = 1/2).
# For element 2, the axis through p_1/p_2 gives a=(-1,7,0)/sqrt(50) at its centroid.
# Element 3 uses anisodir=(1,2,0), hence the current convention gives a=(-2,1,0),
# intentionally not normalized. This tests both direction sources and their fibre tangents.
node 1 coords 3 0.0 0.0 0.0
node 2 coords 3 1.0 0.0 0.0
node 3 coords 3 0.0 1.0 0.0
node 4 coords 3 2.0 0.0 0.0
node 5 coords 3 3.0 0.0 0.0
node 6 coords 3 2.0 1.0 0.0
node 7 coords 3 4.0 0.0 0.0
node 8 coords 3 5.0 0.0 0.0
node 9 coords 3 4.0 1.0 0.0
# A curved quadratic C1 patch with two spans. Its target deformation stretches x by 1.1;
# the last horizontal dof is free, and all other curve dofs prescribe that deformation.
node 10 coords 3 0.0 2.0 0.0 dofidmask 2 1 2
node 11 coords 3 0.25 2.2 0.0 dofidmask 2 1 2
node 12 coords 3 0.75 2.2 0.0 dofidmask 2 1 2
node 13 coords 3 1.0 2.0 0.0 dofidmask 2 1 2
triangularsurface 1 nodes 3 1 2 3 crosssect 1 nlgeo 1
triangularsurface 2 nodes 3 4 5 6 crosssect 2 nlgeo 1
triangularsurface 3 nodes 3 7 8 9 crosssect 3 nlgeo 1 anisodir 3 1.0 2.0 0.0
bsplineplanestrainsurfaceelement 4 nodes 4 10 11 12 13 crosssect 4 knotvectoru 3 0.0 0.5 1.0 degree 1 2 nip 3 nlgeo 1
simplesurfacecs 1 material 1
simplesurfacecs 2 material 2
simplesurfacecs 3 material 3
simplesurfacecs 4 material 4
surfacetensionmat 1 gamma1 0.4 alpha1 0.15 alphas 0.2 mu 0.3 lambda 0.1 checktangent 1.e-5 d 1.0
anisosurfacetensionmat 2 gamma1 0.4 alpha1 0.15 alphas 0.2 mu 0.3 lambda 0.1 eta 0.17 beta 0.13 p_1 3 0.0 0.0 -1.0 p_2 3 0.0 0.0 1.0 checktangent 1.e-5 d 1.0
anisosurfacetensionmat 3 gamma1 0.4 alpha1 0.15 alphas 0.2 mu 0.3 lambda 0.1 eta 0.17 beta 0.13 p_1 3 0.0 0.0 -1.0 p_2 3 0.0 0.0 1.0 checktangent 1.e-5 d 1.0
surfacetensionmat2 4 gamma1 0.4 alpha1 0.15 alphas 0.2 mu 0.3 lambda 0.1 omega1 0.4 omega_ltf 2 useh0 2 h0 0.2 checktangent 1.e-5 d 1.0
BoundaryCondition 1 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 1 values 1 0.0 set 1
BoundaryCondition 2 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 2 values 1 0.0 set 2
BoundaryCondition 3 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 2 values 1 0.2 set 3
BoundaryCondition 4 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 3 values 1 0.0 set 4
BoundaryCondition 5 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 1 values 1 0.025 set 5
BoundaryCondition 6 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 1 values 1 0.075 set 6
NodalLoad 7 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 1 components 1 0.3703353351659955 set 7
NodalLoad 8 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 1 components 1 0.37290193220132717 set 8
NodalLoad 9 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 1 components 1 0.5928088436383351 set 9
# For the IGA dof, differentiate the discrete energy using the same three-point Gauss
# rule in each span, independently of the material implementation:
# E = integral J_ref [W_mem(j/J_ref) + omega/2 (j/J_ref) (H-h0)^2] dxi,
# H = -cross(y_xi,y_xixi)/(2*j^3), j=|y_xi|.
# At u13=.1: dE_mem/du13=.5171084335841627 and dE_bend/du13/omega=-.3497119324883055.
# The two loads therefore preserve the same equilibrium while omega changes from .2 to .4.
NodalLoad 10 loadTimeFunction 1 dofs 1 1 components 1 0.5171084335841627 set 10
NodalLoad 11 loadTimeFunction 2 dofs 1 1 components 1 -0.1398847729953222 set 10
ConstantFunction 1 f(t) 1.0
PiecewiseLinFunction 2 npoints 2 t 2 0.0 2.0 f(t) 2 0.0 1.0
Set 1 nodes 7 1 3 4 6 7 9 10
Set 2 nodes 10 1 2 4 5 7 8 10 11 12 13
Set 3 nodes 3 3 6 9
Set 4 nodes 9 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9
Set 5 nodes 1 11
Set 6 nodes 1 12
Set 7 nodes 1 2
Set 8 nodes 1 5
Set 9 nodes 1 8
Set 10 nodes 1 13
#%BEGIN_CHECK% tolerance 1.e-8
#NODE tStep 1 number 2 dof 1 unknown d value 0.1
#NODE tStep 1 number 5 dof 1 unknown d value 0.1
#NODE tStep 1 number 8 dof 1 unknown d value 0.1
#NODE tStep 1 number 13 dof 1 unknown d value 0.1
#NODE tStep 2 number 2 dof 1 unknown d value 0.1
#NODE tStep 2 number 5 dof 1 unknown d value 0.1
#NODE tStep 2 number 8 dof 1 unknown d value 0.1
#NODE tStep 2 number 13 dof 1 unknown d value 0.1
#%END_CHECK%
